  "_defaults": {
    "character": "club",
    "form": "bumper",
    "tempo": 126,
    "note": "A brief matching no character still gets a real jingle. The default is Club — modern electronic, the sound LoopStar wants to make when nothing in the brief says otherwise. There is no orchestral fallback, by design. See LOOPSTAR_SOUL.md."
  },
  "_fxComment": "Per-character MIX. gain is linear, pan is -1..1, reverb and delay are 0..1 wet. delayNote is a TEMPO-SYNCED division (1/4, 1/8, 1/8d, 1/8t, 1/16) resolved against the piece's BPM at render time — a delay in seconds lands on nothing and is the clearest tell of a preset. lead/pad/drums are the three layers.",
  "soul": {
    "_comment": "The sound identity, machine-readable. Prose lives in LOOPSTAR_SOUL.md; this is the part a planner has to obey. `avoidPrograms` are GM ranges that make LoopStar sound like a 50s game show — fake brass, thin winds, low-resolution bowed strings, clean guitars, novelty. A model asking for one of these gets `substitute` instead, chosen so the GESTURE survives and only the timbre changes.",
    "avoidPrograms": [
      {
        "from": 24,
        "to": 31,
        "why": "clean/acoustic guitars — thin and fake at GM resolution"
      },
      {
        "from": 40,
        "to": 51,
        "why": "bowed strings — low-resolution sample, immediately corny"
      },
      {
        "from": 56,
        "to": 63,
        "why": "brass — the game-show fanfare sound"
      },
      {
        "from": 64,
        "to": 79,
        "why": "winds and reeds — nasal, never edgy"
      },
      {
        "from": 104,
        "to": 119,
        "why": "novelty and world — banjo, bagpipe, steel drum, whistle"
      }
    ],
    "substitute": 1005,
    "_substituteComment": "Fallback lead when a banned program is requested — an app synth voice (programs 1000+ route to LoopStarSynthEngine). Change this id to re-point every rejection at once, no rebuild."
  },
  "_arrangement": {
    "_comment": "How a character is ARRANGED, not just voiced. Before this block existed the composer wrote the same thing for every character: a block triad at MIDI 48 on beats 1 and 3, a melody at MIDI 72, and — only when the piece ran four bars or longer — a kick on 1 and a snare on 3. No bass layer existed at all. That is why a brief asking for a menacing 808 logo measured 0.0% of its energy below 60 Hz.",
    "phraseGenre": "Which pack in frameworks/loopstar/phrases/<genre>/drums.json the beat is borrowed from. 23 genres, 149 authored grooves, none of which a jingle could reach before.",
    "kit": "Kit id from drums/drum-synth-presets.json. BY ID — the binary used to pin index 0.",
    "energy": "0 sparse .. 1 busy. Picks within +/-0.35 in the pack.",
    "leadRegister": "MIDI note the hook is built from. Was hardcoded 72 for everyone.",
    "padRegister": "MIDI note the harmony is voiced from.",
    "padBeats": "Beats in the bar the pad may speak on. [] = no pad. This is how sparse happens.",
    "sub": "The low layer. `anchor` is the tonic's MIDI note — 28 is E1, 33 is A1. Below 24 stops reading as pitch. `program` picks the synth voice: 1000 subSine (pure), 1001 reese (growl), 1002 wobble, 1003 acid.",
    "_gainStaging": "Every layer is peak-normalised to 0.7 before these gains apply, so `gain` is a PEAK ratio and not a loudness one. A sustained sine and a sparse hat pattern that share a peak differ by ~17 dB in RMS. Set sub LOW (0.3-0.5) and drums HIGH (1.3-1.6) or the low end eats the record.",
    "_drumLanes": "Drums render as three lanes — drums (kick/snare/clap/toms/crash), hats (closed/open/ride) and percussion — each peak-normalised on its own and each with its own mix seat. One combined buffer normalised to a 1.25s 808 kick left the sixteenth hats at 0.3% of total energy.",
    "_kitAndSub": "Sub level follows the KIT. trap-808, deep-sub, lofi-thud and boom-bap have long-decay kicks that already own 20-60 Hz, so their sub sits at ~0.16 and the hats come up to compensate. hard-909, rap-knock and pop-punch are tight, so the sub layer is the only low end and sits at ~0.42."
  }
